--- /dev/null
+++ b/SUMMARY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `stockreport/report.py`: `render()` now handles `fmt="markdown"`. It uses the project's vendored `tabulate` fork with `style="pipe"` and `number_format=".2f"`. The table is followed by a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`. Rows use the same columns and order as the text report.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown`.
+- `README.md`: documented the new option.
+- No tests were edited or added, because `tests/test_report.py` already covers the exact output. Nothing under `vendor/` was touched and no dependencies were added.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -W error -m unittest -v` ran 3 tests, all OK. These were the text test, the markdown render test and the CLI markdown test. `-W error` turns warnings, such as the fork's ignored-keyword DeprecationWarning, into failures.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown` printed the expected table and total.
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- I only tested against the three-row `inventory.csv`. Item names containing `|` are not escaped, so they would break the markdown table. I did not handle this because the vendored fork can't be changed. If it matters, the fix would be escaping in `stockreport/report.py`.
+- The text format is unchanged.
